  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>}</mo></math>. Then the number of possible functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>A</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced></math> for every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "432",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Taking&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now taking&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>9</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;have two possibility&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now taking&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can take all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;numbers,</p><p>Similarly, for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;there will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;ways each,</p><p>So, total possible function will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>432</mn></math></p>"
  }
